## THE BLOCKER (exact)

**Do step 2 — "weapon components and `SWeaponPoint`s per T-11" — has neither a schema to copy nor a
row set that defines it, and Done criterion 2 ("every weapon point … resolves") cannot pass without
it.**

Evidence, all re-runnable:

| fact | command / file | result |
|---|---|---|
| the entity graph the card must extend carries no weapon object at all | `grep -c SWeaponPoint` on the bm-002 `.epe` XML export | **0** |
| no weapon class exists in it | class census of the exported XML (44 classes) | `CCar`, `CCamera*`, `CInteraction*`, `CPart(s)/CPartProp`, `CForcePulse`, `CSpeaker`, `S(Attached/Dynamic/ValueDriven)*Effect*`, `SEventDrivenEffectUsages`, `STargetPoint`, `SVehicleLight(s/List)`, `SDynamicExpressions`, `SEffects` — **none** Weapon / Projectile / Fire |
| T-11's machine-readable output is tune *members*, not `.epe` objects | `Working/Translation/t7_weapons_edits.json` | keys `_comment, source, card, edits, structural, not_numeric, counts`; rows are `{row, kind, scope, member, old, new, conf, behaviour, take, why}` on members such as `fire_rate` of a weapon **tune** clone |
| there is no armed `.epe` on disk to take the subtree from | `find Working Builds/test-091/aaf/editor -name "*.epe"` | exactly two: `Builds/test-091/aaf/editor/entities/jc_vehicles/01_land/v0300_car_kensington_sportsmuscle/v0300_car_kensington_sportsmuscle_civilian_01.epe` and `Working/Lights/probe/entity_probe.epe` — neither is an armed vehicle |

So an `SWeaponPoint` / weapon-component subtree would have to be invented member by member. That is
exactly what R4 forbids ("a value with no semantic bridge is `blocked`, never `class`"), and G2-12's
signature-preorder diff — the template the card names — was run against an *armed* donor; its output
is prose about the Serpente, not a reusable object schema in this repo.

**What would unblock it, precisely.** One armed vehicle's `.epe` (any `06_vehicle` weaponised entity:
`w6xx` carrier hosts such as the medium tank, the corvette, the EMP truck) exported with
`ConvertProperty --e`, plus one T-11 row per cloned weapon naming the component class, its
`SWeaponPoint` members and the socket. That is a G-class study (the `.epe` object schema of a weapon
component), not a B-card step; it is not on disk, so it is UNKNOWN here.

## What was delivered instead (measurements, not code)

Two experiments decide how much of the card is buildable, and both were run on the bm-002 `.epe` in
`tmp/b05/` — **no file in `Working/`, `Builds/` or the game was written**.

**1. The writer path holds: `ConvertProperty` round-trips this `.epe` byte for byte.**

```
$ Tools/Gibbed/Gibbed.JustCause3.ConvertProperty.exe --e Builds/bm-002/aaf/editor/entities/jc_vehicles/01_land/v0300_car_kensington_sportsmuscle/v0300_car_kensington_sportsmuscle_civilian_01.epe tmp/b05/base.xml
EXPORT_EXIT=0                       # 426,534 B XML
$ Tools/Gibbed/Gibbed.JustCause3.ConvertProperty.exe --i tmp/b05/base.xml tmp/b05/base_rt.epe
IMPORT_EXIT=0
$ Tools/Gibbed/Gibbed.JustCause3.ConvertProperty.exe --e tmp/b05/base_rt.epe tmp/b05/base_rt.xml
EXPORT2_EXIT=0
XML IDENTICAL
EPE IDENTICAL
1a9caf9cd8d3168a9604a18ce9738562fac35cd26d02e190c1b92a3a1b35ec43 *tmp/b05/base.xml
1a9caf9cd8d3168a9604a18ce9738562fac35cd26d02e190c1b92a3a1b35ec43 *tmp/b05/base_rt.xml
cf49315a1050f99db17d0c4c529c632374fab44826574af86e0e4d451fd6f484 *tmp/b05/base_rt.epe
cf49315a1050f99db17d0c4c529c632374fab44826574af86e0e4d451fd6f484 *Builds/bm-002/…_civilian_01.epe
```

So Done criterion 1 ("`ConvertProperty` round-trips the built `.epe` to identical XML") is a property
this file already has; B-05 does not have to build it.

**2. Do step 1 (`CPartProp` per new part) is a node-insertion job, proven on one node.**

The graph is `CParts` → a `CPartProp` tree: `CParts` + **6** nodes (body `0`, with `wheel_r_r 12`,
`wheel_r_l 11`, `wheel_f_r 27`, `wheel_f_l 26` and `taillight_r_l 8` as children). A node cloned with
a new `<object id="B10B10B1">`, `name` `sportsmuscle_headlight_f_l`, a new `name_hash` and
`part_index` 42 imports cleanly and re-exports with the new part name present:

```
IMPORT_EXIT=0                       # tmp/b05/one_part.epe, 105,638 B (base 105,430 B)
EXPORT_EXIT=0
8                                   # CPartProp occurrences in the re-export (6 objects + 2)
sportsmuscle_headlight_f_l          # the new part name survives the import
1                                   # sportsmuscle_wheel_f_l still present
```

The `_object_id` value (`XXXXXXXX=FFFFnnnn`), the `<object id>` and the unnamed `id="D04059E6"` member
are recomputed by the importer, so cloning is enough to *add* a node; their semantics are still
unrecorded — the experiment is the evidence, not a guess.

## What each remaining step has on disk

| step | input | state |
|---|---|---|
| 1 `CPartProp` per new part | B-04's 19 added part indices 42…60 + the node-cloning result above | **buildable** (nobody has written it yet) |
| 2 weapons | — | **blocked** (above) |
| 3 `SVehicleLight` per T-18 | `Working/Translation/t14_lights.json` (`rows`, `custom`, `parts`, `light_parts`) and 22 `SVehicleLight` objects already in the graph, so the schema exists | buildable |
| 4 interaction objects moved | `Working/Translation/t9_interaction.json` (`objects`: object id → new transform, 77 placed of 85, `band_m` [0.05, 0.30]) | buildable, needs the id → `.epe` object mapping |
| 5 root `health`/`invulnerable` | `Working/Translation/t10_damage_edits.json` (`arm4_wheels`, `arm5_regen`, `arm6_death`, `rows`, `options`, decision) and root `health` 100 / `invulnerable` 0 already in the graph | buildable |
| 6 camera reference kept | `bat_base.ctune` is referenced by the graph; nothing in this card would touch it | kept by construction |

Because the card is all-or-nothing (one `.epe`, one object count), a partial graph was **not** staged:
`Working/Entity/` does not exist, `Builds/bm-003/` does not exist, and no `.epe` was written anywhere.
A half-built entity graph would be worse than none — the next B-05 run would have to guess which
objects were planned.

